; RuleSyntax/JointFirings/Absence: two rules, each makes its kind unless the
; other kind is present.  Absence read at the entry state lets a bag of both
; fire together (both_admitted), a state no run of one match reaches
; (no_run_reaches).  A set store keeps re-deriving a present row a no-change step.
(store set)
(rule add1 (absent (2)) (make (1)))
(rule add2 (absent (1)) (make (2)))
